  "answer": "The goal was not met. The study confirmed four challenging settings: S1, S2, S11 and S28. All four are the nominal setting (1.0x recorded speed, 0 s shift), so none of them shows that a speed\u2013timing combination causes failure. Triage shows that no failure involved the pedestrian. In S1, S2 and S11 the policy drifted or turned left against its route into parked or adjacent vehicles. In S28 the ego was flagged off-road by a small margin, and the triage could not say whether that was the policy's fault. Every off-nominal speed and timing combination that was tried (on 0caa8f1a, 0e002edd and 18f8dbd6) passed. Most of those settings had only one or two runs, though, so they only hint that the combination does not matter. They do not rule it out.",
